{"step_index":168,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T09:15:38Z","input_tokens":12805,"cache_read_tokens":346292,"output_tokens":3117,"thinking":"`v6_sv_comp.py` contains at least three significant bugs. Line 1503-1517, 1584-1599, and 1321 each point to distinct errors in compositing or art direction logic.\n\n\nThe `build_packed_halftone_7px()` function, combined with the `SOFT_LIGHT` blend mode and a halftone factor of 0.34, results in nearly invisible halftone effects in the 1080p compositor. Analysis of the code reveals that the blend mode effectively reduces the contrast of the halftoning, leading to a negligible visual impact. Further investigation is needed to confirm this issue's impact on smooth patches in the image.\n\n\nHalftone effects are imperceptible due to the `SOFT_LIGHT` blend mode's low contrast, which is roughly ten times weaker than expected. High-contrast dots, achieved by adjusting texture ranges and halftone factors, produce crisp and noticeable Spider-Verse-style halftones.\n\nThe `CryptomatteV2` pass is occluded by the translucent `V6_FauxVolumetric_GodRays` effects because the depth setting only records a limited number of object coverage ranks per pixel. This occlusion is problematic when translucent effects or other overlapping elements are rendered in front of objects meant to be identified by Cryptomatte.\n\n\nThe `V6_FauxVolumetric_GodRays` effect appears to be the root cause, as shots with this effect consistently exhibit Cryptomatte occlusion of the car.  Investigating shot parameters (`Pop`, `Car_CMYK`) reveals a correlation between shots where the car drops from Cryptomatte and those that contain the volumetric god rays. Increasing the cryptomatte depth and checking `cry.outputs['Matte']` might reveal if the `CryptomatteV2` setup is the source of the failure. There is a concern about how `CryptomatteV2` is configured, potentially needing a change to `<collection>`, hashes, or `use_pass_cryptomatte_accurate`, depending on whether `cry.outputs['Matte']` returns zero for the car object.\n\n\nThe `Car_CMYK` value correlates with Cryptomatte occlusion in specific shots, suggesting that Kuwahara filtering and CMYK misregistration are blurring the car due to a zeroed-out matte value. Immediate testing of the `cry.outputs['Matte']` in the compositor with a 3-second check will confirm if the `car_matte` is functional or set to `0.0`. Further analysis reveals underexposed/crushed shots alongside clipping artifacts in other scenes.\n\n\nThe hero wheel macro shot appears extremely dark due to dim lighting from the brake heat and car lights on a dark wheel. Enhancing the brake rotor thermal hold and adding a stronger rim-kick light should produce the desired glowing rotor effect. Several other shots are also dark, with low mean luminance and P10 values, indicating underexposure in multiple scenes.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_board","args":{"since":"39"}},{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\nimport bpy, os\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nPROJ = r\\\"D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\"\\nSCRATCH = r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\86052\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\\\scratch\\\"\\nbpy.ops.wm.open_mainfile(filepath=os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"v6_spiderverse\\\", \\\"v6_stage_anim_sv.blend\\\"))\\nsc = bpy.context.scene\\n\\n# 1. Check tunnel vault shadow setting & sun shadow\\nfor nm in (\\\"V6_StrobeTunnel_Vault\\\", \\\"V6_StrobeTunnel_Ribs\\\", \\\"V6_FauxVolumetric_GodRays\\\"):\\n    ob = bpy.data.objects.get(nm)\\n    if ob:\\n        print(f\\\"OBJ {nm}: visible_shadow={getattr(ob, 'visible_shadow', None)} mats={[m.name for m in ob.data.materials if m]}\\\")\\n\\n# 2. Render frame 635 (Act II where Kuwahara size=8.4, mix=0.92!) routing car_matte directly to Composite output -> scratch PNG!\\nng = sc.compositing_node_group\\ncry = [n for n in ng.nodes if n.type == 'CRYPTOMATTE_V2'][0]\\nprint(\\\"CryptomatteV2 node: source=\\\", cry.source, \\\"layer_name=\\\", cry.layer_name, \\\"matte_id len=\\\", len(cry.matte_id), \\\"sample=\\\", cry.matte_id[:120])\\nprint(\\\"Cryptomatte entries count:\\\", len(cry.entries))\\n\\nout_node = [n for n in ng.nodes if n.type in ('COMPOSITE', 'GROUP_OUTPUT')][0]\\n# Save original link, temporarily wire cry.outputs['Matte'] -> out_node.inputs['Image'] at 640x360 to test if car_matte is ZERO or WORKING!\\nsc.camera = bpy.data.objects[\\\"Cam_S12_BankedWallRailCam\\\"]\\nsc.frame_set(635)\\nsc.render.resolution_x = 640\\nsc.render.resolution_y = 360\\nsc.eevee.taa_render_samples = 4\\nng.links.new(cry.outputs['Matte'], out_node.inputs['Image'])\\nmatte_path = os.path.join(SCRATCH, \\\"test_car_matte_635.png\\\")\\nsc.render.image_settings.file_format = 'PNG'\\nsc.render.filepath = matte_path\\nbpy.ops.render.render(write_still=True)\\n\\nim = bpy.data.images.load(matte_path)\\npx = list(im.pixels)[0::4]  # R channel of Matte\\nnz = sum(1 for v in px if v > 0.05)\\nmx = max(px) if px else 0.0\\nprint(f\\\"CAR_MATTE TEST AT f=635: max={mx:.4f}, pixels>0.05 = {nz}/{len(px)} ({100.0*nz/max(1,len(px)):.2f}%)\\\")\\n\"","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\86052\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\\\scratch\\\\test_cryptomatte_and_tunnel.py\""}}]}
